WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.730 line:92%
- It's about to get even more country than this cabin,

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.150 size:75% position:38% line:92%
up in here, alright?

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.980 line:92%
I've got a friend of mine, a guy on the line,

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.250 line:92%
that's going to be joining us.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.180 line:92%
He's super talented singer/songwriter,

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.690 line:92%
who's going to be performing for us a little later as well.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.543 line:92%
Thomas Rhett Akins, you there?

00:00:14.655 --> 00:00:15.499 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What's up?

00:00:15.499 --> 00:00:16.332 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Good.

00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:17.860 line:92%
- I like your hat collection, my man.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.142 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:19.142 --> 00:00:20.213 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:20.213 --> 00:00:21.493 line:92%
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:25.650 line:92%
All right, Thomas Rhett, how's quarantine going at home?

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.420 line:92%
I've been seeing your pictures. They're awesome.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.460 line:92%
- Yeah, we're making the best of it, for sure.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.130 line:92%
We're getting really creative, I guess.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.780 line:92%
With the girls and trying to figure out new ways to have fun

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.590 line:92%
and watching a lot of Disney Plus happening in our house.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.470 line:92%
- Oh my gosh. That's the only two things

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.214 line:92%
my kids say. Disney Plus.

00:00:42.214 --> 00:00:45.170 line:92%
Like, I've had to take their iPad away.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.620 line:92%
I know it's like a way to give them something to do

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.500 line:92%
so you can actually get stuff done, but--

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.333 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:52.000 line:92%
- Man, they are just going nuts right now.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.430 line:92%
Are your kids going nuts?

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:54.410 line:92%
- They're going pretty crazy.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.090 line:92%
Our kids too, like with the iPad, like they get on YouTube

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.160 line:92%
and they go down the worm hole of the kid videos.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:00.993 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yep.

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:01.826 line:92%
- I start looking at them, and I'm like,

00:01:01.826 --> 00:01:03.410 line:92%
what are you even watching?

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:06.260 line:92%
And I'm like, no more iPad. This is not gonna work.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.370 line:92%
- No, I have to take it away.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.180 line:92%
I'm like, I don't know what my little girl is watching,

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.980 line:92%
but all the sudden she became like 16 instead of five.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.240 line:92%
And she has so much attitude.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.540 line:92%
But, it is kind of cool because we're on the road a lot

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:19.610 line:92%
as musicians, so it's kind of cool to be like, at home

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.770 line:92%
and kind of forced into this environment that we don't

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.940 line:92%
generally get to be a part of.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.459 line:92%
And you all just had a baby, right?

00:01:26.459 --> 00:01:27.292 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- We did.

00:01:27.292 --> 00:01:28.125 line:92%
- You all got a fresh one out the oven.

00:01:28.125 --> 00:01:28.958 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- We (laughs) yeah.

00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:31.230 line:92%
She's like, she's a little over two months old.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:32.180 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Her name is Lennon.

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:33.858 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- So pretty.

00:01:33.858 --> 00:01:36.643 line:92%
- And last night she slept from like 11:00

00:01:36.643 --> 00:01:38.050 size:84% position:42% line:92%
to 7:40 in the morning.

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:39.160 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it was--

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:39.993 size:84% position:42% line:92%
- (Kelly whispers) Yes!

00:01:39.993 --> 00:01:41.640 line:92%
- It was absolutely mind blowing.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:42.940 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was amazing.

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:43.970 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.320 line:92%
- Probably one of the best nights of my life, honestly.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:48.690 line:92%
- That is, I totally feel that.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.150 line:92%
It seems like a simple statement,

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:51.862 line:92%
but that's a glorious victory.

00:01:51.862 --> 00:01:52.695 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- It's a big deal.

00:01:52.695 --> 00:01:53.528 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- (Kelly laughs)

00:01:53.528 --> 00:01:54.488 size:78% position:39% line:92%
- Big deal, for sure.

00:01:54.488 --> 00:01:55.321 size:75% position:38% line:92%
- That's a big deal.

00:01:55.321 --> 00:01:57.907 line:92%
Well, I saw you posted a photo of how you handle spit up.

00:01:57.907 --> 00:02:00.950 line:92%
(Dog barks) Oh, sorry, my dog just barked at my husband.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.260 line:92%
So apparently he's evil. - It's okay, our dog--

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:06.490 line:92%
- No, sorry, he was barking.

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:11.490 line:92%
But I saw this photo that you posted and have you just

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:12.470 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
given up on shirts?

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:15.513 line:92%
Because like you've got vomit going down the back of you.

00:02:15.513 --> 00:02:17.810 line:92%
- No, you know what, it's funny is someone asked me that

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:18.643 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
the other day.

00:02:18.643 --> 00:02:20.686 line:92%
They go, "Do you ever wear a shirt?"

00:02:20.686 --> 00:02:23.770 line:92%
And when I'm at home, the answer is not much of the time.

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:24.940 line:92%
Because I guess when I work out of the house

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:26.390 line:92%
and I work out without a shirt on and

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:28.323 line:92%
then I don't shower until, you know, seven o'clock at night.

00:02:28.323 --> 00:02:30.259 line:92%
Just kind of leave the shirt off.

00:02:30.259 --> 00:02:31.092 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:02:31.092 --> 00:02:32.270 line:92%
- Especially when I'm holding the baby, I mean there's no

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.320 line:92%
point in ruining, you know, eight shirts during the day.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.440 line:92%
I think my wife changes about 17 times

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:37.546 size:81% position:41% line:92%
just from spit up, so.

00:02:37.546 --> 00:02:40.220 line:92%
- Oh my gosh. I gave up on nice things.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.690 line:92%
I just own black or white.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.030 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I'm just like, whatever.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:46.070 line:92%
So I saw a video showing you outdoors,

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:48.150 line:92%
while you are quarantining.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.290 line:92%
What were you doing in a tree?

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:51.570 line:92%
Like I saw this video of you

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:53.623 line:92%
like trying to swing like Tarzan.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:55.737 line:92%
What was the deal with that?

00:02:55.737 --> 00:02:57.810 line:92%
- We just moved into a new house

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.480 line:92%
and we were kind of exploring outside

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:02.500 line:92%
and my wife noticed this vine hanging from the tree

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.460 line:92%
and my kids were trying to swing on it

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:06.540 line:92%
and Lauren was like, I used to do that when I was little.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.876 line:92%
She was like let me go try it

00:03:07.876 --> 00:03:09.290 line:92%
and I said "how about you let me go try it first

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.420 line:92%
just to make sure that it's like stable."

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.150 line:92%
And so I like yanked on it a couple of times

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:14.930 line:92%
and it felt fine and then I like went for it,

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:17.530 line:92%
and the limb just snapped in half and I think

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.840 line:92%
I bruised my tailbone and I'm really embarrassed

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:22.740 line:92%
that Lauren caught that on video, but you know,

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.730 line:92%
that's just what we do around here.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:27.250 line:92%
- Is your wife there? Is that who you keep looking at?

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:28.692 line:92%
- Yeah, she is. You want to come over here?

00:03:28.692 --> 00:03:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Hey, what's up?

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.330 line:92%
- She was doing the girls' hair.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.651 size:84% position:42% line:92%
- Oh, making it pretty?

00:03:33.651 --> 00:03:34.484 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Hey.

00:03:34.484 --> 00:03:36.510 line:92%
- Hi. Do your girls ask for braids?

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.530 line:92%
My girl asks for braids all the time.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.690 line:92%
- Yes, Elsa braids. Elsa and Anna braids,

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:41.777 line:92%
is what they call them. - Exactly.

00:03:41.777 --> 00:03:43.450 line:92%
And I keep telling my girl, like you don't have

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.530 size:75% position:38% line:92%
that hair yet. Okay?

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.360 line:92%
Like I can do a braid, but you ain't got that.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:47.540 line:92%
That's not happening yet.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.730 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, that's amazing.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:53.000 line:92%
Hey, well how are you doing as a mamma? This is a lot.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.620 line:92%
- Yeah. Honestly, we're good.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:59.785 line:92%
We're going on like 30, or no, 40 something days

00:03:59.785 --> 00:04:00.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- 40 days.

00:04:00.618 --> 00:04:02.870 line:92%
Quarantine because our kids had the flu the week before

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.057 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
coronavirus hit, so

00:04:05.057 --> 00:04:05.890 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.710 line:92%
- But my sister and her husband live close by,

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:10.790 line:92%
and my best friend lives close by, and they all were able

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:13.160 line:92%
to work from home like super early on, so they were like

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.860 line:92%
we're going to come quarantine at your house.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:15.890 line:92%
So they have been here - Oh

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:19.970 line:92%
- I think they said yesterday it was 34 days.

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:20.980 size:88% position:44% line:92%
That they had been here.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:22.460 line:92%
- We've had a lot of help, which has been nice.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.437 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And a lot of (mumble).

00:04:23.437 --> 00:04:24.870 line:92%
- I was going to say, that's incredibly cool because

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.740 line:92%
I was going to say you all being like, I know you have

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.210 line:92%
already been parents but a baby is a lot,

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:33.098 line:92%
and especially in this time. - It's tough.

00:04:33.098 --> 00:04:35.020 line:92%
That's a lot just to get, and I know that sounds horrible,

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.360 line:92%
but every parent's thinking it.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.870 line:92%
Sometimes you just need to be alone.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:39.703 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Without them.

00:04:39.703 --> 00:04:41.660 line:92%
- Just to like come back and be fresh

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.897 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and not hate your life.

00:04:43.897 --> 00:04:44.980 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Absolutely.

00:04:47.105 --> 00:04:50.030 line:92%
- We've had lots of extra sets of hands around.

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.730 line:92%
To hold the baby, while somebody cooks or entertain

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.540 line:92%
the toddlers, or you know.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.745 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- That's so cool.

00:04:56.745 --> 00:04:57.620 line:92%
- It's been fun. Lots of games.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:58.453 line:92%
- Well, that's kind of cool.

00:04:58.453 --> 00:05:00.235 line:92%
You've got your own quarantine community.

00:05:00.235 --> 00:05:01.265 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I like that.

00:05:01.265 --> 00:05:02.098 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:05:03.087 --> 00:05:05.250 line:92%
- So, you studied to be a nurse, right, Lauren?

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.010 line:92%
And I heard you celebrated Thomas' 30th birthday

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:10.060 line:92%
by surprising some nursing students.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.630 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That was cool.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:13.130 size:84% position:42% line:92%
- We did. It was sweet.

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:14.440 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was fun.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:16.180 line:92%
- How did that come about?

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.650 line:92%
- I'd stayed connected with the nursing school.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:22.720 line:92%
I went to the University of Tennessee in Knoxville.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.400 line:92%
And I have just stayed really close with that community

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.400 line:92%
and they were like would you all mind calling in and just

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.750 line:92%
encouraging some of the students and, I mean,

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:33.020 line:92%
I can't imagine, my brother is actually a senior this year

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:38.020 line:92%
at UT and I just can't imagine that being in college and

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:42.480 line:92%
especially in high school, there's so many like last things

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.780 line:92%
that so many kids - Yeah, that are kind of

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.900 line:92%
getting ripped away from people. Yeah.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.790 line:92%
- But I do think people are doing a really good job at just

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.213 line:92%
finding creative ways to celebrate.

00:05:53.223 --> 00:05:56.530 line:92%
It will definitely be for all these students such an

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.695 line:92%
unforgettable senior year.

00:05:58.695 --> 00:05:59.820 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah, for sure.

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:03.220 line:92%
- It was cool to get to at least try to encourage.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:04.053 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We have no idea

00:06:04.053 --> 00:06:05.830 line:92%
what they are feeling, but I'm sure,

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:07.080 line:92%
there's so many unknowns.

00:06:09.208 --> 00:06:11.260 line:92%
- It was nice because it was a thoughtful thing.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:14.320 line:92%
And I think that the, for everybody like that putting their

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.320 line:92%
life on the line right now for us.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.277 line:92%
That's a lot to ask of a human.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:19.110 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- It is.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:20.170 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- And a heart.

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:22.370 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I love your love story.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:26.640 line:92%
Would you tell it for us? Tell everyone how you met.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:29.203 line:92%
And where you were like, he's the one, Lauren.

00:06:30.925 --> 00:06:32.225 line:92%
- It was one summer night.

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:37.824 line:92%
- No but you all were really young.

00:06:37.824 --> 00:06:40.380 line:92%
- We have known each other for a really long time.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:42.238 line:92%
- Like how long? Tell everyone how long you all have

00:06:42.238 --> 00:06:43.216 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
known each other.

00:06:43.216 --> 00:06:44.945 line:92%
- We've known each other- - First grade.

00:06:44.945 --> 00:06:46.040 line:92%
- First grade - Technically

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:47.020 line:92%
- We started going to school together.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:48.440 line:92%
I don't really know how much you can know somebody

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:49.273 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in first grade.

00:06:49.273 --> 00:06:51.540 line:92%
- Yeah, it was middle school when we like really got

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.950 line:92%
to be close, hung out a whole lot more,

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:58.100 line:92%
and church camp was kind of the start of the friendship

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.530 line:92%
in middle school, but then it just--

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:01.750 line:92%
- Watch out for church camp.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.047 line:92%
That's where people be making out.

00:07:03.047 --> 00:07:04.297 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- That's right.

00:07:05.527 --> 00:07:08.985 line:92%
- Finding the Lord and a girlfriend.

00:07:08.985 --> 00:07:11.530 line:92%
- Yeah, there's a picture of us somewhere, of me and Lauren

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.420 line:92%
at church camp. I think we were fifth grade, sixth grade.

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:15.986 line:92%
But I was like a foot shorter than Lauren was.

00:07:15.986 --> 00:07:16.819 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:07:16.819 --> 00:07:20.610 line:92%
- And I dyed my hair black because I was in this like punk

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:24.430 line:92%
rock band and, you know, I just was obsessed with her

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:27.230 line:92%
and I'm sure she looked at me like "yeah, probably not."

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:31.670 line:92%
But we became really good friends that year and actually

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:33.420 line:92%
dated a little bit when we were 16.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:36.413 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- It wasn't good.

00:07:36.413 --> 00:07:40.150 line:92%
- I was a needy boyfriend. If that makes any sense.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:41.830 size:84% position:42% line:92%
- Well, you're also 16.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:44.540 line:92%
So you're still like in puberty too.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:45.890 line:92%
- Exactly. Figuring it out.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.930 line:92%
- Did everybody tell you it was not

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:50.248 line:92%
gonna work out because that's

00:07:50.248 --> 00:07:51.120 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Absolutely.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.940 line:92%
- That's weird that it did. It's awesome.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.190 line:92%
- Yeah, so we broke up but still remained

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:58.890 line:92%
really good friends and both dated other people from

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:00.816 size:78% position:39% line:92%
us five or six years.

00:08:00.816 --> 00:08:03.950 line:92%
Through all of that time, we went on double dates together

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.547 line:92%
with other people that we were dating.

00:08:05.547 --> 00:08:07.720 line:92%
- He would come stay with me and my roommates in college.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.250 line:92%
Because he went to a school in Nashville and we were

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:12.600 line:92%
in Knoxville which is roughly a three hour drive.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.700 line:92%
So on the weekends, he would come up and go to games

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.190 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and stay with us.

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:19.560 line:92%
And I think a couple of times he stayed with my boyfriend,

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:20.624 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
we just-

00:08:20.624 --> 00:08:22.480 line:92%
- (Laughing) I love this.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:26.600 line:92%
- Yeah. We are a very tight knit circle we run with so.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.050 line:92%
- Lauren, I also wanted to bring this up because you

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:30.980 line:92%
just wrote a book called "Live in Love" about your life

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:32.483 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and family.

00:08:32.483 --> 00:08:33.890 line:92%
So what made you want to write it?

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:36.290 line:92%
Because that's a lot to let people in your life.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:37.603 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yep. It is.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:43.830 line:92%
You know, I think marrying him was a pretty big leap

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:47.330 line:92%
of faith as far as knowing which direction he was trying

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.433 size:81% position:41% line:92%
to go with his career.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:55.730 line:92%
His whole world is super out of my box and so writing a book

00:08:56.090 --> 00:09:00.770 line:92%
was not something that I ever had like on my dream checklist

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:04.180 line:92%
but I did I wanted to share my story.

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:06.670 line:92%
I was encouraged to share my story.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:10.740 line:92%
I didn't think I would ever would in this capacity

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:15.740 line:92%
but I actually went in to my agency's office just to talk

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:19.620 line:92%
through possibly writing a children's book because we were

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:22.123 line:92%
in the process of adopting Willa Gray.

00:09:23.422 --> 00:09:24.363 line:92%
And they were like it would be cool if you wrote

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:26.720 line:92%
a children's book that had to do with Africa,

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:27.890 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
African themed,

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.980 line:92%
so we kind of went in talking about that and she was like

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:32.090 line:92%
well tell me a little about yourself.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.020 line:92%
As I was like talking through how I was raised and some

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:38.420 line:92%
of the stories throughout my life and kind of what had led

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:42.470 line:92%
me to where I was now, I'm pretty sure she had cried

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.940 line:92%
like three times throughout me telling my story.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:46.200 line:92%
I was like is this normal?

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.090 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- It moved her.

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:50.247 line:92%
- And she was like wiping her eyes

00:09:50.247 --> 00:09:51.120 line:92%
and she was like that's it.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:53.150 line:92%
Like you have to tell that story first.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.020 line:92%
We'll get to children's books later.

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:57.293 size:84% position:42% line:92%
But I was like, really?

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:01.160 line:92%
And our manager, who is one of our very best friends,

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:03.200 line:92%
she was like, Lauren, I've been telling you for awhile

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.740 line:92%
you need to be writing this stuff down.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:07.763 line:92%
There's so many good stories in your life.

00:10:09.098 --> 00:10:11.440 line:92%
So that's really what started it.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:13.890 line:92%
It turned into a full-on book.

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:16.160 line:92%
- It's about your life and kind of how you've handled it

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:17.750 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and navigated it, right?

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.154 line:92%
- Right. - Living in love.

00:10:19.154 --> 00:10:24.110 line:92%
- Marriage and our kids, adoption, biological.

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.130 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How I was raised.

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:28.180 line:92%
Kind of what our life is like now.

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:29.980 line:92%
It was a really therapeutic process,

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:30.880 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
going back through

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:32.690 line:92%
all of that. - For both of us. Sure.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:33.523 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- I'll bet.

00:10:33.523 --> 00:10:35.811 line:92%
- But it was good. It's scary.

00:10:35.811 --> 00:10:39.100 line:92%
I would be lying if I told you I wasn't anxious

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:41.770 line:92%
and nervous about this coming out, just because it is

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:42.603 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
really personal.

00:10:42.603 --> 00:10:43.860 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's really honest.

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:48.750 line:92%
And this is so not my comfort zone, just being in this world

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.620 line:92%
and being super vulnerable to people

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:52.700 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that you may never meet.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:56.720 line:92%
But it's been a really cool, I've been surprised at how cool

00:10:56.720 --> 00:11:00.470 line:92%
the process has been, and how excited I do feel, although

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.760 line:92%
the nerves are still definitely there.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:05.230 line:92%
- Connecting to people through your book is such a powerful

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:07.520 line:92%
thing because a lot of people go through things

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:11.170 line:92%
with blended families and everybody's from a different kind

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:13.555 line:92%
of place, and that can be very hard.

00:11:13.555 --> 00:11:14.820 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- For sure.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:16.400 line:92%
- Why did you adopt first?

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:17.780 line:92%
You adopted first, right?

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:21.100 line:92%
- We did. I had always talked about adopting my whole life.

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:22.843 line:92%
My mom is actually adopted.

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:26.850 line:92%
I just thought it was really cool, so we talked about it

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:30.270 line:92%
off and on but it wasn't something that we had sat down

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:32.773 line:92%
and had a like a full-on adoption conversation.

00:11:34.625 --> 00:11:37.757 line:92%
And then I was in Uganda in 2016

00:11:39.325 --> 00:11:40.158 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:11:40.158 --> 00:11:44.070 line:92%
- And I had a picture of one of the babies there.

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:47.970 line:92%
And I had shared it on social media

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.420 line:92%
and when I finally got to FaceTime him that night

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:54.470 line:92%
I was telling him her story and I was like, "Babe, we know

00:11:54.470 --> 00:11:58.030 line:92%
so many people who are trying to adopt right now

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:01.077 line:92%
and this little girl needs a forever home."

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:06.150 line:92%
I was like so moved I mean the second I touched her

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:09.030 line:92%
it was like electric and I was like "oh, my word.

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:11.860 line:92%
This little girl has just taken my heart."

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:14.840 line:92%
And I was like, "Honey, we have got to find her her forever

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:17.850 line:92%
home," like I know that's why I'm here is to get this girl

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:18.893 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to her home.

00:12:20.984 --> 00:12:21.934 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Oh, my God. Okay.

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:25.220 line:92%
You totally Oprah-ed me just now.

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:26.563 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm like, okay.

00:12:27.493 --> 00:12:30.263 line:92%
I did my own make up and this is not waterproof.

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:33.370 line:92%
Like it's so beautiful because I know that feeling

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:35.980 line:92%
because the moment you touch them or hold somebody

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:37.960 line:92%
it doesn't matter if it's yours or not.

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:39.110 size:84% position:42% line:92%
We're a blended family.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:42.300 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is my purpose.

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:43.790 line:92%
It's such a powerful thing.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:44.964 size:78% position:39% line:92%
- For sure. For sure.

00:12:44.964 --> 00:12:47.114 line:92%
- So how did that turn into ya'll adopting?

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.360 line:92%
- When I talked to her on the phone that night

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:52.800 line:92%
and she said we needed to find her a home, I literally,

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:55.380 line:92%
it was after a concert, and I was going to bed,

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.842 line:92%
and I was like, "we'll bring her home."

00:12:57.842 --> 00:12:59.850 line:92%
And I don't fully remember even saying it.

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:03.440 line:92%
It was like such a spiritual thing for me that it just

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:04.950 size:75% position:38% line:92%
came out of my body.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:08.840 line:92%
And then literally two weeks after, we were having home

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:12.930 line:92%
assessments and talking to adoption agencies and then

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:15.140 line:92%
I got to go to Uganda maybe

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:15.973 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- October

00:13:15.973 --> 00:13:18.060 line:92%
- Yeah, like six months later.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.800 line:92%
And then I got to meet her for the first time and that's

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:22.290 line:92%
when we really started the process and we were--

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:26.320 line:92%
Lauren was there for like a total of a very long time.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:29.040 line:92%
And I was going to Uganda, I remember I played a show in

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:31.870 line:92%
Phoenix, Arizona and flew from Phoenix to Uganda,

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.610 line:92%
stayed for a week, came back home, played Nashville,

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:36.080 line:92%
and then came right back to Uganda.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.850 line:92%
And it was like this really, really strange time

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:43.510 line:92%
of like I'm still doing touring things and Lauren is

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:45.690 line:92%
in the middle of all of this and then fast-forward like

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:48.453 line:92%
three months later we're pregnant in Uganda.

00:13:49.372 --> 00:13:52.460 line:92%
- (laughing) - Ugandan toilets

00:13:54.035 --> 00:13:56.030 line:92%
- I remember playing the Nashville show and I was talking

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:57.200 line:92%
to her and I was like "what are you doing?"

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:58.980 line:92%
And she was like "I'm currently just yacking in the toilet."

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.230 line:92%
She's like, "what are you doing?"

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.680 line:92%
Well, I'm hanging out with all of your best friends

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:02.513 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in Nashville.

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:05.300 line:92%
You'll see this in the book.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:06.680 line:92%
Like I look like a total jerk.

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:07.513 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- No.

00:14:07.513 --> 00:14:09.110 line:92%
- Seventeen million times in the book.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:11.650 line:92%
And I probably am a lot of the time.

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:14.038 line:92%
- You're also doing your job, like that's how you provide.

00:14:14.038 --> 00:14:14.871 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:14:14.871 --> 00:14:15.704 line:92%
- Provide for your family.

00:14:15.704 --> 00:14:17.511 line:92%
And then I just got to say before I move on to something

00:14:17.511 --> 00:14:18.480 line:92%
else I love about you all.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:20.950 line:92%
It's a really beautiful thing that I think I believe that

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:22.860 line:92%
things in life are supposed to happen when they happen.

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:24.490 line:92%
Like regardless if it's good or not.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:26.580 line:92%
It's just how it is and you handle it.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:29.090 line:92%
And I love how you said "It was just something

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:29.923 size:81% position:41% line:92%
that came out of you."

00:14:29.923 --> 00:14:32.540 line:92%
Because I think that says a lot about both of your hearts,

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:35.137 line:92%
it's that you noticed there was a need for something

00:14:35.137 --> 00:14:36.393 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and you fulfilled it.

00:14:36.393 --> 00:14:37.226 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:14:37.226 --> 00:14:38.993 line:92%
- And it wasn't a question.

00:14:38.993 --> 00:14:41.160 line:92%
you know, it was like this just needs to happen.

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.490 line:92%
I think that's a really beautiful thing and how we should

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:44.920 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
live our lives.

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:47.190 line:92%
All right, so Thomas the song that you're going to do for us

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:48.940 line:92%
later is called "Be a Light."

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:50.660 line:92%
It's a great anthem for the world right now,

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:52.020 line:92%
like how did this song come about?

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:53.950 line:92%
I know there's a lot of artists on it, right?

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.690 line:92%
- Yeah. I actually wrote this song last year

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:58.660 line:92%
in a whole different mind set, like having no clue

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:01.720 line:92%
that COVID-19 was about to hit the world.

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:02.600 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:04.700 line:92%
- So it was going to kind of be on like our next album

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:06.440 line:92%
that we're going to start working on at some point

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:08.770 line:92%
in the near future, hopefully, but just when all of this

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:10.887 line:92%
started happening I called my label and I was like,

00:15:10.887 --> 00:15:12.660 line:92%
"Hey, I think this song needs to come out now.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:14.870 line:92%
Like I think the world needs to hear this song."

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:16.670 line:92%
Because it's a really encouraging song just about being

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:18.710 line:92%
a light in a dark place, and I kind of think that's

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:21.040 line:92%
kind of the world we're in right now.

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:23.450 line:92%
So we decided to put it out and we got Reba on it,

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:26.300 line:92%
Keith Urban, Chris Thomlin, and Hillary Scott

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:29.383 line:92%
are singing on it with me, which was super special

00:15:29.383 --> 00:15:31.830 line:92%
and a bunch of the proceeds are going to the Music Cares

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.720 line:92%
COVID Relief Fund, which is really cool.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:37.640 line:92%
So whether you stream it on any platform or YouTube it

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:41.797 line:92%
or download it that money will go to help a lot

00:15:41.797 --> 00:15:43.300 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of the people.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:45.430 line:92%
- All right. Well thank you guys so much.

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:47.610 line:92%
We are going to get to hear Thomas Rhett sing later

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:49.357 line:92%
in the show, very excited about that.

00:15:49.357 --> 00:15:51.240 line:92%
The song is called, "Be a Light."

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:52.510 line:92%
So please go download it now

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:54.650 line:92%
and also go order Lauren's book.

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:55.750 line:92%
You can pre-order it right now.

00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:59.180 line:92%
It's called "Live in Love" or you can get it August 18.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:00.830 line:92%
It's a great, great message.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:03.580 line:92%
You're going to love it. You're going to connect to it.

